##vso[task.logissue type=warning;sourcepath=objects/rules/covert-spray-rule-0242.yaml;linenumber=45;columnnumber=271;code=eql_expression_depth;]expression nesting exceeds 250 levels (parentheses plus chained `not`/`-`/`+`): Elasticsearch 8.19.17+, 9.3.5+, 9.4.3+, and 9.5 reject this query; earlier patches and 9.0 to 9.2 accept it%0Ahelp: the EQL reference: https://www.elastic.co/docs/reference/query-languages/eql
##vso[task.logissue type=warning;sourcepath=objects/rules/covert-tunnel-rule-0088.yaml;linenumber=62;columnnumber=13;code=kql_unscoped_union;]unscoped `union` uses wildcard table `*` and reads every table; name the tables instead (https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/kusto/query/best-practices)%0Ahelp: the KQL reference: https://learn.microsoft.com/kusto/query/
##vso[task.logissue type=warning;sourcepath=objects/rules/elevated-beacon-rule-0200.yaml;linenumber=71;columnnumber=349;code=esql_expression_depth;]expressions nest 310 deep; Elasticsearch 8.19.17+, 9.3.5+, 9.4.3+, and 9.5 reject more than 300 (earlier releases allow 400)%0Ahelp: the ES|QL reference: https://www.elastic.co/docs/reference/query-languages/esql
##vso[task.logissue type=warning;sourcepath=objects/rules/elevated-downgrade-rule-0251.yaml;linenumber=59;columnnumber=17;code=lucene_unescaped_slash;]`/var/` is read as a regular expression because `/` is unescaped, so the value splits into separate clauses; escape the slashes (`\/`) or quote the value%0Ahelp: the Lucene query string reference: https://www.elastic.co/docs/reference/query-languages/query-dsl/query-dsl-query-string-query
##vso[task.logissue type=warning;sourcepath=objects/rules/elevated-harvest-rule-0362.yaml;linenumber=63;columnnumber=21;code=eql_nested_comment;]Elasticsearch nests block comments, so this comment runs past its first `*/`; other EQL tools end it there. Avoid `/*` inside a comment%0Ahelp: the EQL reference: https://www.elastic.co/docs/reference/query-languages/eql
